{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"301036e40fc6d9a1793ec1abdbd7536f8417d17d19e4d5c09d7d30fb2ff1ee26","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_c12a8891a4eacb40ce63fb968f03e84537740a87b131d24d180983808603ba71","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technical deep learning framework for small-scale data. The supplied text does not contain a broader impact statement, ethics discussion, or specific data compliance documentation. The authors are identified by name and affiliation, and the paper cites prior work by the same authors, but no frozen policy or external evidence is available to determine if these constitute violations.","paper_id":"BysZhEqee","paper_identity_sha256":"aad247b49587da4c99e5bea2b98fccbe0f3a4d3f890be4627a6bb6e19997980b","prompt_identity_sha256":"8bda984bb36036b3fcb6452fd5903c3e4c040abbccb71a75186b20326abed588","raw_response_sha256":"fde94505d2cc436ae692f33c8337e0d1b48f3b0b073b12be7e509b1e96c275c5","request_identity_sha256":"64e12712f18fcffd26d76b93ee0428a8c221c44fbdb690e8061823e0921d4845","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"93c9a9c4921144d72358f2c46c49405d2d38cd37a0bbb16540430efcd51eea80","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not contain a dedicated section or discussion regarding ethical risks, fairness, bias, or potential harms associated with the proposed Marginal Deep Architectures (MDA). The application domains mentioned (e.g., handwritten digits, speech recognition) do not explicitly raise material ethical concerns in the text, but the absence of any ethical consideration or mitigation strategy is noted.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-030"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes several public datasets (USPS, Isolet, Sensor, Covertype, Ibnsina, CIFAR-10, CMU mocap) and provides URLs for their sources. However, the text does not explicitly state the licensing terms, consent protocols, or privacy compliance measures for these datasets. While these are standard public benchmarks, the paper lacks specific documentation of adherence to data usage policies or licensing requirements.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors' names (Yuchen Zheng, Guoqiang Zhong, Junyu Dong) and their institutional affiliation (Ocean University of China) on the title page. It also provides direct email addresses. Without a frozen venue policy confirming double-blind requirements for this specific submission, these details are described as visible identifiers. They would typically compromise anonymity in a double-blind review context, but no policy violation is declared due to the lack of frozen policy evidence.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-014"],"review_text":"The paper cites prior work by the same authors (Zheng et al., 2014; 2015) regarding stacked feature learning models and deep architectures. The text states that the proposed framework is based on these previous works. The supplied evidence does not contain information regarding dual submission or specific textual overlap that would constitute plagiarism. The absence of external overlap evidence means originality and dual submission status cannot be determined from the paper text alone.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or any documentation of IRB/ethics approvals. There is no discussion of the societal implications of the model or specific compliance with external policy obligations regarding impact statements. The supplied paper-only evidence is insufficient to determine if such documentation was required or if its absence constitutes a policy violation.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL